 "stimulus_html": "Looking again at the <a href=\"https://openstax.org/r/Chapter8_Data-Sets\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">\"InState\"</a> dataset, answer these questions.",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 529192,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "What tuition is at the 10th percentile?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>You want the tuition at the 15<sup>th</sup> percentile.</p>\n<p>Open a copy of the file in Google Sheets. You cannot edit the original file.</p>\n<p>Look for the InState tab.</p>\n<p>Look for the Tuition column.</p>\n<p>In a blank cell, enter the function: =PERCENTILE(</p>\n<p>Click on the letter at the top of the Tuition column.</p>\n<p>Then enter a comma, the percentile as a decimal and close the parentheses: ,0.1)</p>\n<p>The complete function probably looks like this: =PERCENTILE(C:C,0.1)</p>\n<p>The tuition you see is $3,120.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "$3,120\n"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 529193,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "What tuition is at the fourth quintile?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Quintiles measure in fifths, or in steps of 20%. The fourth quintile is the 80<sup>th</sup> percentile. You want the tuition at the 80<sup>th</sup> percentile.</p>\n<p>Open a copy of the file in Google Sheets. You cannot edit the original file.</p>\n<p>Look for the InState tab.</p>\n<p>Look for the Tuition column.</p>\n<p>In a blank cell, enter the function: =PERCENTILE(</p>\n<p>Click on the letter at the top of the Tuition column.</p>\n<p>Then enter a comma, the percentile as a decimal and close the parentheses: ,0.8)</p>\n<p>The complete function probably looks like this: =PERCENTILE(C:C,0.8)</p>\n<p>The tuition you see is $26,465.20.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "$26,465.20"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 529194,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "At what percentile is the main campus of New Mexico State University (in-state tuition: $6,686)?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Open a copy of the file in Google Sheets. You cannot edit the original file.</p>\n<p>Look for the InState tab.</p>\n<p>Look for the Tuition column.</p>\n<p>In a blank cell, enter the function: = PERCENTRANK(</p>\n<p>Click on the letter at the top of the Tuition column.</p>\n<p>Then enter a comma, 6686, and close the parentheses: ,6686)</p>\n<p>The complete function probably looks like this: =PERCENTRANK(C:C,6686).</p>\n<p>You see the decimal value 0.323.</p>\n<p>Convert this to a percentage to say that this is the 32.3<sup>rd</sup> percentile.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "32.3rd"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 529195,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "At what percentile is Bowdoin College in Maine (in-state tuition: $53,922)?",
